<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to June 9 to offset the widening effect of a fall in current accounts in francs, which was only partly compensated by a rise in bank notes circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   447.51 (+  0.56)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  15.84 (-  3.55)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.14 (-  0.19)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   25.79 (   unch)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 117.48 (+  2.62)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   476.25 (+  1.00)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
